From 46fda089d2e9da58c891f56fb93a76becb9a4545 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EscapeA <escapea@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 01:56:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(webview): declare color-scheme meta so Android WebView
 honors web theme in dark mode
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

hermes-studio ships its own prefers-color-scheme dark theme, but without
<meta name="color-scheme" content="dark light"> Android WebView's
FORCE_DARK (DARK_STRATEGY_PREFER_WEB_THEME_OVER_USER_AGENT_DARKENING)
cannot detect that the page supports a dark theme, so it falls back to
UA algorithmic darkening — inverting images/icons (negative look).

Adding the meta tag lets WebView evaluate prefers-color-scheme normally;
the page then applies its own dark theme and icons keep their colors.
---
 packages/client/index.html | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/packages/client/index.html b/packages/client/index.html
index 6f5afdb4..ef57e8f3 100644
--- a/packages/client/index.html
+++ b/packages/client/index.html
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
 
 <head>
   <meta charset="UTF-8" />
+  <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark light" />
   <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.ico" />
   <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/logo.png" />
   <link rel="manifest" href="/manifest.webmanifest" />
-- 
2.53.0

